    {
      "id": "xdsih9z",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Directed Graph (Digraph): edges have direction (u → v ≠ v → u)",
        "Undirected Graph: edges have no direction; u–v = v–u",
        "Weighted Graph: edges have weights/costs",
        "Degree: in-degree (edges coming in), out-degree (edges going out) for directed graphs",
        "Path: sequence of vertices connected by edges",
        "Cycle: path that starts and ends at same vertex",
        "DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph): directed graph with no cycles — used in compilers, task scheduling"
      ]
    },
