    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w7mmbqj",
      "content": "<strong>Note: </strong><em>Quick Sort is fastest in practice (cache-friendly); Merge Sort is best for linked lists &amp; external sorting; Heap Sort is always O(n log n) in-place.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Time and space complexity analysis using Big-O notation is heavily tested in GATE and Indian CS competitive exams.",
        "Tree traversals (Inorder, Preorder, Postorder) and binary tree properties are standard calculation questions.",
        "Distinction between array dynamic bounds vs linked list memory allocation is frequently evaluated."
      ],
      "id": "p3pn1va"
